IO-46: read groundwater flow from a runoff interface file as a rate per unit area

subcatch_getResults() saves a subcatchment's groundwater outflow as a total
flow, gw->newFlow * area, in flow units. runoff_readFromFile() put it back
into gw->newFlow converted only to cfs, but gw->newFlow is a flow per unit
area (ft/s): addGroundwaterInflows() multiplies it by the area again. It also
never moved gw->newFlow to gw->oldFlow, which addGroundwaterInflows()
interpolates from. Divide by the area and shift the old value, as
gwater_getGroundwater() does in the run that wrote the file.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-46_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c b/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
index bf00bad..ae14425 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
@@ -465,7 +465,12 @@ void  runoff_readFromFile(void)
         gw = Subcatch[j].groundwater;
         if ( gw )
         {
-            gw->newFlow    = SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_GW_FLOW] / UCF(FLOW);
+            // --- file holds total flow; gw->newFlow is flow per unit area
+            gw->oldFlow    = gw->newFlow;
+            gw->newFlow    = 0.0;
+            if ( Subcatch[j].area > 0.0 )
+                gw->newFlow = SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_GW_FLOW] / UCF(FLOW) /
+                              Subcatch[j].area;
             gw->lowerDepth = Aquifer[gw->aquifer].bottomElev -
                              (SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_GW_ELEV] / UCF(LENGTH));
             gw->theta      = SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_SOIL_MOIST];
